        "id": 13029,
        "name": "Heckbringer",
        "username": "Heckbringer",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/58956e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-05-18T19:10:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>In the second paragraph of The Sentinels' backstory, it says this: \"<span>So, when a crazed time traveling pirate appeared outside a restaurant they were at on a double-date, the giant of a man and the man made of living energy were the ones to stop her and toss her into her own time portal.\"</span></p><p>Then in the sixth paragraph, it says this: \"<span>&nbsp;In the main lobby, a bizarre portal opened to another time, and a rakish woman stepped through, proclaiming herself to be Maria Helena Teresa Fafila Servanda Jimena Mansuara Paterna Domenga Gelvira Placia Sendina Belita Eufemia Columba Gontina Aldonza Mafalda Cristina Tegrida de Falcon and demanding the secrets of...\"</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Seems to me like the same person since \"a crazed time traveling pirate\" sounds like a decent (though not terribly charitable) way of referring to La Capitan (who is refered to by&nbsp;<em>that</em> name later on), but in that second meeting it doesn't reference the first at all, and doesn't make it sound like they recognize her.</p><p>Thoughts? Revelations? Canon?</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:43.418Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 6,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 30.0,
        "yours": false,
